From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SenkOS
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 18:40:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: rtw88: sdio: drop RX packets that run past the read
 buffer

rtw_sdio_rxfifo_recv() trusts the RX descriptor's packet length. On the
RTL8821CS a descriptor sometimes claims more than the RX FIFO held
(seen: 1554 bytes in a 256 byte read), and skb_put() then BUGs in the
SDIO IRQ thread, which takes Wi-Fi down for good:

  skbuff: skb_over_panic: ... len:1554 put:1554 ... tail:0x652 end:0x140
  kernel BUG at net/core/skbuff.c:214!
  Call trace:
   skb_put+0x5c/0x60
   rtw_sdio_rx_skb+0x50/0xe0 [rtw88_sdio]
   rtw_sdio_rxfifo_recv+0x244/0x2a8 [rtw88_sdio]

Check the length against what was read and drop the rest of the read
instead.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/sdio.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/sdio.c b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/sdio.c
index 5b40d74b1..fec03664a 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/sdio.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/sdio.c
@@ -1008,6 +1008,18 @@ static void rtw_sdio_rxfifo_recv(struct rtw_dev *rtwdev, u32 rx_len)
 		curr_pkt_len = ALIGN(pkt_offset + pkt_stat.pkt_len,
 				     RTW_SDIO_DATA_PTR_ALIGN);
 
+		/* The descriptor may claim more than the FIFO held (a partial
+		 * or corrupted entry): skb_put() would BUG and take the SDIO
+		 * IRQ thread with it, so drop what is left of this read.
+		 */
+		if (pkt_offset + pkt_stat.pkt_len > rx_len) {
+			dev_warn_ratelimited(rtwdev->dev,
+					     "RX packet of %u bytes at offset %u past the %u read\n",
+					     pkt_stat.pkt_len, pkt_offset, rx_len);
+			dev_kfree_skb_any(skb);
+			return;
+		}
+
 		if ((curr_pkt_len + pkt_desc_sz) >= rx_len) {
 			/* Use the original skb (with it's adjusted offset)
 			 * when processing the last (or even the only) entry to
